#### RT-03: Broken ~/.codex/models_cache.json: syntax error and valid-but-not-an-object
- **(a) Implements case:** **NO** ([`test_readiness.py:138-164`](file:///home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/tests/test_readiness.py#L138-L164)). The test bundles passing sub-runs (Run A syntax error and Run C permission denied) with failing sub-runs (Run B array) under a single `@pytest.mark.xfail(strict=True, raises=AssertionError)`. Because `cache_result` raises `AssertionError` at [`test_readiness.py:160`](file:///home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/tests/test_readiness.py#L160), the loop terminates early: `qwen_result` is never asserted, and the syntax error / permission denied assertions are masked under the expected failure wrapper.
- **(b) CAN IT FAIL:** **YES (on fix/mutation)**. Currently, the test expects to fail and produces `XFAIL`. If [`readiness.py:98`](file:///home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/readiness.py#L98) and [`readiness.py:147`](file:///home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/readiness.py#L147) are fixed to guard array payloads (`isinstance(d, dict)`), the test completes without raising `AssertionError`, turning red as `XPASS (strict)` at [`test_readiness.py:138`](file:///home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/tests/test_readiness.py#L138). Without fixing the script, any mutation that crashes Run A or Run C with an `AssertionError` remains green as `XFAIL`.
- **(c) Avoids real machine/quota:** **YES** ([`test_readiness.py:138-164`](file:///home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/tests/test_readiness.py#L138-L164)). Isolated files in `tmp_path`, no network calls.

